  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Seven straight wins is not a sequence. It's a test of whether close games stop feeling lucky.",
    "what_this_means": "Pivetta lasted four innings. The bullpen inhaled after he exhaled. Manny Machado hit one into the gap. The kind of moment that separates a W from the narrow loss this team knows too well. Two runners converted at-bat into runs when it mattered. The pitching held a two-run margin into the ninth. Yuki Matsui closed it. This is balanced baseball with no margin for error and no time to stop and think about it. The Padres aren't surfing momentum. They're executing under pressure so consistently that close feels normal now. In a division chase, normal close wins are the only ones that count.",
    "what_to_watch": "Tomoyuki Sugano's ERA sits at 5.30. Colorado's offense has struggled against moving fastballs all month. Tonight the Padres send Casey Mize to the mound in a ballpark that rewards precision over power.",
